[
  {
    "role": "intro",
    "text": "For a given segment of a circle, to complete the circle, the very one of which it is a segment. Let $ABC$ be the given segment of a circle. So it is required to complete the circle for segment $ABC$, the very one of which it is a segment."
  },
  {
    "role": "construction",
    "text": "For let $AC$ be cut in half at (point) $D$ [Prop.~1.10],",
    "construction_cite": "1.10",
    "objects_introduced": ["$D$"]
  },
  {
    "role": "construction",
    "text": "and let $DB$ be drawn from point $D$, at right-angles to $AC$ [Prop.~1.11].",
    "construction_cite": "1.11",
    "objects_introduced": ["$DB$"]
  },
  {
    "role": "construction",
    "text": "And let $AB$ be joined.",
    "construction_cite": null,
    "objects_introduced": ["$AB$"]
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "Thus, angle $ABD$ is surely either greater than, equal to, or less than (angle) $BAD$.",
    "assertion": "angle ABD is greater than, equal to, or less than angle BAD",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "Thus, "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "angle $ABD$ is surely either greater than, equal to, or less than (angle) $BAD$"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": "."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "First of all, let it be greater.",
    "assertion": "case 1: angle ABD is greater than angle BAD",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "First of all, let it be "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "greater"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": "."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "construction",
    "text": "And let (angle) $BAE$, equal to angle $ABD$, be constructed on the straight-line $BA$, at the point $A$ on it [Prop.~1.23].",
    "construction_cite": "1.23",
    "objects_introduced": ["$BAE$"]
  },
  {
    "role": "construction",
    "text": "And let $DB$ be drawn through to $E$,",
    "construction_cite": null,
    "objects_introduced": ["$E$"]
  },
  {
    "role": "construction",
    "text": "and let $EC$ be joined.",
    "construction_cite": null,
    "objects_introduced": ["$EC$"]
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "Therefore, since angle $ABE$ is equal to $BAE$, the straight-line $EB$ is thus also equal to $EA$ [Prop.~1.6].",
    "assertion": "EB is equal to EA",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "Therefore, since "},
      {"label": "assumption", "text": "angle $ABE$ is equal to $BAE$"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": ", "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "the straight-line $EB$ is thus also equal to $EA$"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": " [Prop.~1.6]."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": "1.6"
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "And since $AD$ is equal to $DC$, and $DE$ (is) common, the two (straight-lines) $AD$, $DE$ are equal to the two (straight-lines) $CD$, $DE$, respectively.",
    "assertion": "the two straight-lines AD, DE equal the two straight-lines CD, DE respectively",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "And since "},
      {"label": "assumption", "text": "$AD$ is equal to $DC$"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": ", and "},
      {"label": "assumption", "text": "$DE$ (is) common"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": ", "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "the two (straight-lines) $AD$, $DE$ are equal to the two (straight-lines) $CD$, $DE$, respectively"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": "."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "And angle $ADE$ is equal to angle $CDE$. For each (is) a right-angle.",
    "assertion": "angle ADE is equal to angle CDE",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "And "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "angle $ADE$ is equal to angle $CDE$"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": ". For "},
      {"label": "assumption", "text": "each (is) a right-angle"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": "."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "Thus, the base $AE$ is equal to the base $CE$ [Prop.~1.4].",
    "assertion": "the base AE is equal to the base CE",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "Thus, "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "the base $AE$ is equal to the base $CE$"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": " [Prop.~1.4]."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": "1.4"
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "But, $AE$ was shown (to be) equal to $BE$. Thus, $BE$ is also equal to $CE$.",
    "assertion": "BE is equal to CE",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "But, "},
      {"label": "assumption", "text": "$AE$ was shown (to be) equal to $BE$"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": ". Thus, "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "$BE$ is also equal to $CE$"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": "."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "Thus, the three (straight-lines) $AE$, $EB$, and $EC$ are equal to one another.",
    "assertion": "the three straight-lines AE, EB, EC are equal to one another",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "Thus, "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "the three (straight-lines) $AE$, $EB$, and $EC$ are equal to one another"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": "."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "Thus, if a circle is drawn with center $E$, and radius one of $AE$, $EB$, or $EC$, it will also go through the remaining points (of the segment), and the (associated circle) will be completed [Prop.~3.9].",
    "assertion": "a circle drawn with center E and radius AE goes through all the points and the circle is completed",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "Thus, "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "if a circle is drawn with center $E$, and radius one of $AE$, $EB$, or $EC$, it will also go through the remaining points (of the segment), and the (associated circle) will be completed"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": " [Prop.~3.9]."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": "3.9"
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "Thus, a circle has been completed from the given segment of a circle.",
    "assertion": "a circle has been completed from the given segment of a circle (case 1)",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "Thus, "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "a circle has been completed from the given segment of a circle"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": "."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "And (it is) clear that the segment $ABC$ is less than a semi-circle, because the center $E$ happens to lie outside it.",
    "assertion": "the segment ABC is less than a semi-circle",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "And (it is) clear that "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "the segment $ABC$ is less than a semi-circle"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": ", because "},
      {"label": "assumption", "text": "the center $E$ happens to lie outside it"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": "."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "[And], similarly, even if angle $ABD$ is equal to $BAD$, (since) $AD$ becomes equal to each of $BD$ [Prop.~1.6] and $DC$, the three (straight-lines) $DA$, $DB$, and $DC$ will be equal to one another.",
    "assertion": "case 2 (ABD equal BAD): the three straight-lines DA, DB, DC are equal to one another",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "[And], similarly, even if "},
      {"label": "assumption", "text": "angle $ABD$ is equal to $BAD$"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": ", (since) "},
      {"label": "assumption", "text": "$AD$ becomes equal to each of $BD$ [Prop.~1.6] and $DC$"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": ", "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "the three (straight-lines) $DA$, $DB$, and $DC$ will be equal to one another"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": "."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": "1.6"
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "And point $D$ will be the center of the completed circle.",
    "assertion": "point D will be the center of the completed circle",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "And "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "point $D$ will be the center of the completed circle"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": "."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "And $ABC$ will manifestly be a semi-circle.",
    "assertion": "ABC will be a semi-circle",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "And "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "$ABC$ will manifestly be a semi-circle"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": "."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "And if $ABD$ is less than $BAD$, and we construct (angle $BAE$), equal to angle $ABD$, on the straight-line $BA$, at the point $A$ on it [Prop.~1.23], then the center will fall on $DB$, inside the segment $ABC$.",
    "assertion": "case 3 (ABD less than BAD): the center will fall on DB, inside the segment ABC",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "And if "},
      {"label": "assumption", "text": "$ABD$ is less than $BAD$"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": ", and we construct (angle $BAE$), equal to angle $ABD$, on the straight-line $BA$, at the point $A$ on it [Prop.~1.23], then "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "the center will fall on $DB$, inside the segment $ABC$"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": "."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": "1.23"
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "And segment $ABC$ will manifestly be greater than a semi-circle.",
    "assertion": "segment ABC will be greater than a semi-circle",
    "spans": [
      {"label": "glue", "text": "And "},
      {"label": "assertion", "text": "segment $ABC$ will manifestly be greater than a semi-circle"},
      {"label": "glue", "text": "."}
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "conclusion",
    "text": "Thus, a circle has been completed from the given segment of a circle. (Which is) the very thing it was required to do."
  }
]

